{
  "name": "Inner Magic",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "LUEpcQatUgKGRnnU",
  "img": "icons/magic/nature/moon-crescent.webp",
  "folder": "vzMm8Zi2FMbA8Ep4",
  "sort": 200000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Magic within you can enhance your body or mind. When you finish a Long Rest, choose one of the following benefits; it lasts until you choose another. As a Bonus Action, you can switch to a different benefit, a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Ardor.</strong> You have Advantage on Charisma ability checks and on saving throws to avoid or end the Frightened condition.</p><p><strong>Mobility.</strong> Your Speed increases by 10 feet, and climbing and swimming don't cost you extra movement.</p><p><strong>Vigor.</strong> You gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you have Advantage on Strength (Athletics) and Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-5QG9SDf6xVHJ3EAF\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Each activity applies its benefit (Vigor also gives the Temporary Hit Points); remove the previous benefit's effect yourself. After a Long Rest, the choice is free: use the activity and restore the use. The Advantage against Frightened is not automated.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
